## FILE 1 — `terraform/ssl_certs.tf`

**Action: DELETE everything in this file and replace with the content below.**

```hcl
# The ArgoCD certificate is already present in Key Vault (uploaded manually or via pipeline).
# We read it here via a data source — no PFX file or password secret required on disk.
#
# IMPORTANT: If this is the FIRST TIME and the cert does NOT yet exist in KV,
#            upload it manually first:
#   az keyvault certificate import \
#     --vault-name kvcfsettlacceuwaks001 \
#     --name argocd-settlement-acc-tennet-cloud \
#     --file ssl_certs/argocd.settlement.acc.tennet.cloud.pfx \
#     --password "<pfx-password>"
#
data "azurerm_key_vault_certificate" "argocd_ssl_certificate" {
  count = local.argocd_domain_is_present ? 1 : 0

  name         = replace(local.aks.argocd_domain, ".", "-")
  key_vault_id = data.azurerm_key_vault.aks_kv.id
}
```

